cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the ground-truth data, please cite it as below."
title: "LLM Processing of Historical Accounting Book Data — JSONtoRDF"
abstract: >-
  Encoding transcribed medieval accounting book entries from the Cistercian monastery of
  Aldersbach into RDF/XML with an LLM, and evaluating the result against a manually
  encoded ground truth. Reduced, standalone extract of the Aldersbach Digital pipeline.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Vogeltanz
    given-names: Maximilian
    affiliation: "University of Graz"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - digital humanities
  - historical accounting books
  - RDF
  - linked open data
  - large language models
  - Latin
repository-code: "https://github.com/MaxVogeltanz/LLMProcessing_HistoricalAccountingBookData"
